cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this package, please cite it and the associated manuscript.
  postexportKinetics is released on GitHub and has no DOI of its own; its
  intended future distribution channel is Bioconductor. The DOI
  10.5281/zenodo.22944109 identifies the frozen manuscript implementation
  (postexport-kinetics, tag manuscript-revision-v1.0), listed under
  references; it is not the DOI of this package.
type: software
title: "postexportKinetics: Kinetic Model Comparison for Post-Export RNA Conversion"
version: "0.1.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bioinformatics-sannio/postexportKinetics"
url: "https://github.com/bioinformatics-sannio/postexportKinetics"
authors:
  - family-names: "Faretra"
    given-names: "Luca"
  - family-names: "Napolitano"
    given-names: "Francesco"
  - family-names: "Pancione"
    given-names: "Massimo"
  - family-names: "Cerulo"
    given-names: "Luigi"
    email: "lcerulo@unisannio.it"
abstract: >-
  R package for compartment-resolved four-state kinetic modelling of nuclear
  and cytoplasmic, unprocessed and processed RNA. It implements a
  constrained nested-model comparison between a null model without a
  post-export conversion rate and a full model with a non-negative
  post-export conversion rate. Estimation uses trapezoidal interval
  balances, propagated and regularised covariance and whitened non-negative
  least squares; inference uses a replicate-level generative bootstrap with
  an add-one p-value. The package also provides simulation, design
  diagnostics against the manuscript benchmark, multiple-testing adjustment,
  exploratory ranking and plots. The post-export conversion rate is a
  phenomenological parameter and does not identify a specific molecular
  mechanism. First public GitHub release; not a Bioconductor release.
keywords:
  - RNA kinetics
  - post-export conversion
  - compartment-resolved RNA
  - transcriptomics
  - kinetic modelling
  - bootstrap inference
  - R package
